.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt YACC 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm yacc
.Nd generate a C LALR(1) parser (bounded POSIX core)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dv
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Ar grammar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a yacc grammar and writes a C parser.
The declarations support
.Li %token ,
.Li %left ,
.Li %right ,
.Li %nonassoc ,
.Li %start
and
.Li %prec .
The parser uses LALR(1) tables, resolves shift/reduce conflicts with precedence and
associativity, and implements the
.Li error
token with panic-mode recovery.
Semantic values are
.Li int ;
.Li %union
and typed actions are outside this bounded core.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Write the token header as
.Pa y.tab.h
(or the output name with a
.Pa .h
suffix).
.It Fl v
Write the rule and conflict counts to standard error.
.It Fl o Ar file
Write the parser to
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa y.tab.c .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width y.tab.h
.It Pa y.tab.c
Default parser output.
.It Pa y.tab.h
Token header with
.Fl d .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lex 1
.Sh BUGS
.Li %union ,
.Li %type ,
.Li $<field>
references, mid-rule actions,
.Li %destructor ,
.Li %locations ,
.Li %expect
and
.Li %define
are not supported.
The generated parser uses an
.Li int
semantic value.
